        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Nottingham, England\n- Systems: Royal Centre tram stop, Nottingham Trent University tram stop\n- Organizations: Nottingham Trent University\n- Places: Victoria Centre, Cornerhouse\n- Buildings: Newton Building, Arkwright Building\n- Products: Aqua Horological Tintinnabulator, Victoria Centre Clock, Emett Clock, The Time Fountain\n\nFacts:\n- Intu Victoria Centre is a shopping centre in Nottingham, England, that was constructed between 1967 and 1972.\n- The Aqua Horological Tintinnabulator, also known as the Victoria Centre Clock, the Emett Clock, and The Time Fountain, is a water-powered clock in Nottingham, England.\n- Royal Centre tram stop is close to the Cornerhouse, the Victoria Centre, and the Newton Building of Nottingham Trent University.\n- Much of Nottingham Trent University's City Campus is closer to Nottingham Trent University tram stop than to Royal Centre tram stop.\n- Nottingham Trent University tram stop is near the university's flagship Arkwright Building and Newton Building to the south.\n- The Newton Building is closer to Royal Centre tram stop than to Nottingham Trent University tram stop.",
